s Faculty & Staff Community & Fans More Admission Info Why UTulsa Research Opportunities Virtual Tour Explore the City of Tulsa Explore Programs Visit Apply Business, cyber security undergrads named 2025 Gilman Scholars The University of Tulsa is proud to announce two recent recipients of Benjamin A. Gilman International Scholarships: Eden Knepper and Ayden Whittaker. Each year, the U.S. Department of State awards the nationally competitive Gilman awards... More Student Info Course Bulletin IT Help Research Opportunities Student Orgs Student Hub Housing Portal Academic Calendar Cultivating cultural conversations: Meet UTulsa’s Professor Lansana Quraysh Ali Lansana, applied associate professor of English & creative writing, is a distinguished scholar of African American studies, journalist and author of 23 books including poetry, nonfiction and children’s literature. His journey as a writer led him from Enid, Oklahoma, to studying and teaching in cities like Chicago and New York. However, after 30 […] More Family Info About UTulsa UTulsa Leadership & Faculty Explore the City of Tulsa UTulsa Merchandise & Gifts University School Resources for Parents & Families Parent & Family Portal Get Involved New alumnus offered elite IBM cybersecurity position months before graduation Serving nontraditional students, such as military veterans, is nothing new at The University of Tulsa, and Don Cowan’s success is a prime example of how students from all backgrounds thrive on campus. Humble and soft-spoken, Cowan (B.S. ’25) graduated from Owasso High School and served eight years as a U.S. Marine before returning to Tulsa […] More Alumni Info Alumni Benefits Request Transcripts TU Merchandise & Gifts TU Alumni Association TU Alumni Events Kendall College welcomes television and film writer Taylor Chukwu to Board of Visitors The University of Tulsa Kendall College of Arts & Sciences has welcomed alumna Taylor Chukwu as the newest member of its Board of Visitors. More Employee Info Employee Benefits IT Help Applications Directory Hurricane Hub Employment Opportunities Seagraves leads national charge in AI-powered real estate innovation UTulsa assistant professor Cayman Seagraves is leading the charge toward integrating AI into the real estate and finance sectors. More Community Info TU Athletics 101 Archer Gilcrease Museum Calendar of Events Campus Maps Life Long Learning Mellon Foundation grants $677,000 for new UTulsa, Muscogee (Creek) Nation project UTulsa has received a $677,000 grant from the Public Knowledge program of the Mellon Foundation to support a joint effort between the university and the Muscogee (Creek) Nation’s Historic and Cultural Preservation Department. New alumnus offered elite IBM cybersecurity position months before graduation July 16, 2025 Serving nontraditional students, such as military veterans , is nothing new at The University of Tulsa, and Don Cowan’s success is a prime example of how students from all backgrounds thrive on campus. Humble and soft-spoken, Cowan (B.S. ’25) graduated from Owasso High School and served eight years as a U.S. Marine before returning to Tulsa in 2021 to earn his bachelor’s degree in cybersecurity . His capstone project was conducted in partnership with the university’s Oklahoma Cyber Innovation Institute . Cowan benefited from multiple internships, including one with IBM in Austin, Texas, last summer. By September, the global technology corporation had offered him a full-time job at the elite IBM X-Force Red upon graduation. Cowan will be conducting ethical hacking to identify gaps in organizations’ security controls and protect IT systems from potential attacks. “I’ve always been fascinated by building things and taking them apart to discover ways they can work differently than intended,” he said. “To me, penetration testing is like solving multiple puzzles at once, but instead of following a picture on a box, I’m finding unexpected ways the pieces fit together. It’s an interesting blend of creativity and problem-solving where thinking ‘wrong’ often leads to important discoveries.” As an undergraduate, Cowan worked in the on-campus Information Technology Security Operations Center, which offers prime jobs to the best cyber students to defend the university from online threats. He also served as president of the Root 66 Cyber Club and participated in multiple penetration testing and cyber defense competitions. Cowan thanked all of his professors in the College of Engineering & Computer Science for their support and gave a special mention of Codi West , Ph.D., who serves as an instructional assistant professor of cyber studies and director of co-curricular activities. “Don has been an amazing student to work with. He has made the most of every opportunity we could provide, from captaining competitive learning teams to co-developing lab infrastructure,” said Tyler Moore , Ph.D., who serves as the Tandy Endowed Chair in Cyber Security and Information Assurance and chair of the School of Cyber Studies . “I’m excited for Don to join several fellow UTulsa alumni at IBM X-Force Red.” All Posts , Alumni , Cybersecurity , Engineering & Computer Science , Experiential Learning , Featured , Internships , Jonathan Codi West , News , Stories , Student Experiences , Student Stories , Tyler Moore Colleges Arts & Sciences Business Engineering & Computer Science Graduate School Health & Natural Sciences Honors College Law News & Media Events Subscribe Link to Facebook Link to Twitter Link to Instagram Link to YouTube Link to Snapchat Link to LinkedIn Visit Apply Employment Offices Newsroom Technical Help Contact The University of Tulsa © 2026 The University of Tulsa 800 S. Tucker Drive Tulsa, OK 74104 Accreditation Accessibility Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Social Media Policy"
    }
